.TH elfshaker-pack 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-pack \- Combine loose snapshots into a compressed pack.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker pack\fR [\fB\-T\fR|\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-compression\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-frames\fR] [\fB\-\-snapshots\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-snapshots0\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPACK\fR> [\fIINDEX\fR]... 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a compressed pack and pack index from loose snapshots. By default, all loose snapshots are included. Select snapshots with positional indexes, \-\-snapshots\-from, or \-\-snapshots0\-from.
.PP
The source loose snapshots and objects remain in the data directory. Use elfshaker gc to remove redundant loose data after the pack is created.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 0]
Use N compression workers; 0 selects the number of physical CPU cores.
.TP
\fB\-\-compression\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR [default: 10]
Use Zstandard compression LEVEL (up to 22); negative values select fast compression.
.TP
\fB\-\-frames\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 0]
Write N independent compression frames. More frames permit more parallel decompression but may reduce compression. 0 selects approximately one frame per 512 MiB of input.
.TP
\fB\-\-snapshots\-from\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read newline\-delimited snapshot names from FILE; use \- for standard input.
.TP
\fB\-\-snapshots0\-from\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read NUL\-delimited snapshot names from FILE; use \- for standard input.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPACK\fR>
Name of the pack to create.
.TP
[\fIINDEX\fR]...
Loose snapshot indexes to include.
